  "body": "Sibling of #4563, named and left alone by its patch (ggbdpq's \"provider: a Claude sign-in whose keychain write fails leaves logins.json alone\").\n\nThat patch moves `addLogin`'s `writeLogins(upsertLogin(ls, l))` to after the credential write, so a failed `putClaudeLogin` (Keychain or file) leaves logins.json as it was. `switchSavedLogin` (`internal/provider/logins.go`, line 1199 at c30d3b7b6) still writes logins.json, with the `On` marks moved to the new login, before it writes the credential with `putClaudeLogin`. If that write fails (a Keychain refusing `security add-generic-password`, a read-only `.credentials.json`), logins.json says the new login is on while Claude Code still runs as the old one, and the GUI's account list shows the wrong account as in use.\n\nFix: write the credential first and the `On` marks after it succeeds, as `addLogin` now does, with a test like `TestClaudeLoginKeychainWriteFailureKeepsLoginsFile`: a fake `security` that fails on PATH in a sandbox HOME, and logins.json's bytes the same after the failed switch.\n\nFrom reading the code. Not reproduced.\n",
