     "body": "Found while building the cswap import (64cdb6803, #4532).\n\nOn mote over ssh, one imported Claude account failed its Keychain write. It was still added to magpie, so importing the same file again reported it as already there.\n\nThe cause: `addLogin` writes `logins.json` before it signs Claude Code in, and it doesn't undo that write when the sign-in fails. Every import and every sign-in goes through this path, not just cswap.\n\nFix: write the login only after the credential is stored, or roll it back on failure. Add a test with a failing Keychain write that checks logins.json is unchanged. The test must fail on the current code.",
