   "body": "Fixed on [fix/4592-claude-switch-credential-first](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/4592-claude-switch-credential-first), commit [ec847e8b](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/ec847e8b57547260ea435db9e36e249b2f987482), based on upstream `ed0ab567`.\n\nThe shared Claude switch path now keeps the outgoing login changes in memory, writes the new credential, and saves `logins.json` only after that succeeds. Codex ordering is unchanged.\n\nA regression through public `SwitchLogin` uses an isolated HOME and fake keychain that rejects the credential write. On the base the saved login file changes; with the fix its exact bytes remain, the refusal reaches the caller, and the credential is attempted once. Successful switches and refreshed outgoing credentials remain covered by the existing tests. Focused provider tests pass with `-race`, vet/build pass, and macOS test compilation passes. I independently reran the failure and successful-switch tests.\n\nNo real keychain, live credential or full suite was used. A later login-record failure after credential success can still leave stores divergent, as with the existing `addLogin` ordering; this change adds no transactional rollback. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
